cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived results, please cite the manuscript listed below."
title: "Expression-level immune signatures outperform gene-set enrichment scores for predicting immune checkpoint inhibitor response: a cross-cohort benchmark in 591 patients"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived results for a head-to-head benchmark of 27
  strategies for constructing a transcriptomic immune score, evaluated under an
  identical scoring, discrimination and pooling procedure across six independent
  ICI-treated cohorts (591 patients, 127 responders) with TCGA-HNSC (520 primary
  tumours) as the discovery cohort. Scores built from gene-level expression
  consistently outperformed scores built from gene-set enrichment statistics.
